WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.963
Here's what you'll be able to
do by the end of this module.

2
00:00:02.963 --> 00:00:06.912
You'll explain why Quick Access is a
bridge that should shrink to nothing.

3
00:00:06.912 --> 00:00:11.090
You'll build a Private Access
application: bound to a connector group,

4
00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:16.074
with only the segments it uses, a group
assignment, and a Conditional Access policy.

5
00:00:16.074 --> 00:00:20.711
You'll say where connector groups go,
including for applications in A W S,

6
00:00:20.711 --> 00:00:23.775
Google Cloud and Oracle
Cloud Infrastructure.

7
00:00:23.775 --> 00:00:26.025
You'll put administrative hosts behind the

8
00:00:26.025 --> 00:00:28.463
phishing-resistant
authentication strength.

9
00:00:28.463 --> 00:00:32.554
And you'll describe the domain
controller sensor's audit-first order,

10
00:00:32.554 --> 00:00:34.062
and run Learn's klist test.

11
00:00:34.062 --> 00:00:36.974
You need Module 2; Module
3 isn't needed here,

12
00:00:36.974 --> 00:00:42.049
because the compliant network check
doesn't apply to Private Access apps.

13
00:00:42.049 --> 00:00:46.263
Read Network and Transport,
chapter five, on Private Access.

14
00:00:46.263 --> 00:00:49.490
The lab runs in a test
tenant, never production.
